eq": 1, "word_index": 12, "context": "Inspired by her close connection to nature , she has explored the remotest corners of the continent and is active in the fight to protect African elephants", "context_len": 27}}}, "wildlife": {"freq": 11, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 11, "word_index": 30, "context": "The next morning , we hooked up with Ishmail , a local guide who took us on game viewing expedition on the river , a great opportunity to observe the wildlife from a unique vantage point", "context_len": 36}}}, "balloonist": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 18, "context": "Joining us on the expedition are location manager , Marc Baar , field engineer , Hal Bowker and balloonist , Dany Cleyet Marrel", "context_len": 23}}}, "lightweight": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 12, "context": "So , in the context of the parrot-rifle performance benchmark , the lightweight hybrid cannon matched up , which just leaves the Irish question", "context_len": 24}}}, "ballooning": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 8, "context": "Dany is one of the world 's leading ballooning expert", "context_len": 10}}}, "expeditions": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 4, "context": "scientific hot air balloon expeditions on all continents and is the inventor of a wide range of flying devices used in the famous canopy raft missions", "context_len": 26}}}, "continents": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 29, "context": "If the lord almighty wanted colored people to mix with whites , to live with whites , to marry whites , he would n't ha placed them on separate continents", "context_len": 30}}}, "canopy": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 23, "context": "scientific hot air balloon expeditions on all continents and is the inventor of a wide range of flying devices used in the famous canopy raft missions", "context_len": 26}}}, "canyons": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 15, "context": "A short distance from the dunes , we drive east through some of the oldest canyons on earth , the gateway to one of last safe havens for the elusive black rhino", "context_len": 32}}}, "havens": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 26, "context": "A short distance from the dunes , we drive east through some of the oldest canyons on earth , the gateway to one of last safe havens for the elusive black rhino", "context_len": 32}}}, "poaching": {"freq": 7, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 11, "context": "Numbering in the hundreds of thousands a century ago , illegal poaching caused their population to dwindle to less than 2500", "context_len": 21}, "VERB_PresC": {"freq": 5, "word_index": 22, "context": "Well , the vicar 's maid cleans the place and the Colonel threatened to chuck that Archer bloke back into chokey for poaching", "context_len": 23}}}, "dwindle": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 16, "context": "Numbering in the hundreds of thousands a century ago , illegal poaching caused their population to dwindle to less than 2500", "context_len": 21}}}, "rhinos": {"freq": 11, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 10, "word_index": 12, "context": "A number of private game reserves in Africa have been restocked with rhinos", "context_len": 13}, "VERB_PresT": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 8, "context": "Extremely skittish and fearful of poachers , black rhinos spend most of their time hidden in thick bush", "context_len": 18}}}, "keratin": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 12, "context": "Thought to have healing powers , rhino horn is in fact mere keratin , the same substance as our fingernail", "context_len": 20}}}, "medicinal": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 4, "context": "This protein has zero medicinal value , yet it is pushing a magnificent species to the brink of extinction", "context_len": 19}}}, "extinction": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 18, "context": "This protein has zero medicinal value , yet it is pushing a magnificent species to the brink of extinction", "context_len": 19}}}, "restocked": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 10, "context": "A number of private game reserves in Africa have been restocked with rhinos", "context_len": 13}}}, "skittish": {"freq": 4, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 4, "word_index": 1, "context": "Extremely skittish and fearful of poachers , black rhinos spend most of their time hidden in thick bush", "context_len": 18}}}, "poachers": {"freq": 4, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 4, "word_index": 15, "context": "A nearby radio tower used by the scientists could be spotted on Google Earth enabling poachers to find the location , so we have been asked not to show any pictures of the surrounding area", "context_len": 35}}}, "forks": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 10, "context": "I think just up ahead here is where the road forks", "context_len": 11}}}, "plateau": {"freq": 4, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 4, "word_index": 11, "context": "Leaving the Canyon region , we head west to the Waterberg plateau , the home of the Cheetah Conservation research center and one of the largest protected habitats for the fastest predator on earth", "context_len": 34}}}, "inaccessible": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 6, "context": "Most of the delta is totally inaccessible by car , so the best way to appreciate this piece of Eden is from the air", "context_len": 24}}}, "rangers": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 30, "context": "On the express condition that we do not reveal our actual location , we 've received special permission to penetrate deep into a rhino sanctuary accompanied by heavily armed anti-poaching rangers", "context_len": 31}}}, "enabling": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 14, "context": "A nearby radio tower used by the scientists could be spotted on Google Earth enabling poachers to find the location , so we have been asked not to show any pictures of the surrounding area", "context_len": 35}}}, "sighting": {"freq": 5, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 5, "word_index": 18, "context": "I ca n't believe it , we 've been here less than an hour and already our first sighting", "context_len": 19}}}, "reclusive": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 7, "context": "Unlike white rhinos , black rhinos are reclusive solitary animals , seldom seen during the day", "context_len": 16}}}, "waterholes": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 14, "context": "But they do need to drink daily , so they usually head for the waterholes after sunset", "context_len": 17}}}, "infra": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 18, "context": "The next morning , with the help of the Cheetah Conservation Fund researchers who monitor cheetah activity with infra red camera traps , we head for an area where several predators have been spotted earlier in the day", "context_len": 38}}}, "jackal": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 1, "context": "A jackal , a leopard , a white rhino , all in a few minutes", "context_len": 15}}}, "leopard": {"freq": 5, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 5, "word_index": 4, "context": "Contrary to lion and leopard who from time to time may be a threat to humans , cheetah represent no danger to people , but they do kill domestic animals and are considered vermin by the local farmers", "context_len": 38}}}, "calf": {"freq": 8, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 8, "word_index": 14, "context": "So we decide to take the time to follow a mother elephant and her calf in the bush", "context_len": 18}}}, "tablet": {"freq": 4, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 4, "word_index": 22, "context": "I ca n't rest or sleep or anything , till I just rush off up here and write it down in that tablet", "context_len": 23}}}, "habitats": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 27, "context": "Leaving the Canyon region , we head west to the Waterberg plateau , the home of the Cheetah Conservation research center and one of the largest protected habitats for the fastest predator on earth", "context_len": 34}}}, "cheetahs": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 20, "context": "I have done a lot of work with lions and hyenas , but I never had a chance to observe cheetahs at such close range in the wild before", "context_len": 29}}}, "specimens": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 6, "context": "About half of the 6000 remaining specimens are found in Namibia", "context_len": 11}}}, "spanning": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 8, "context": "This predator has a large hunting range often spanning over 150 km", "context_len": 12}}}, "safaris": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 5, "context": "In Southern Africa , photo safaris often take place in fenced-in games reserves that have been re-stocked with wild animals", "context_len": 20}}}, "antelope": {"freq": 5, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 5, "word_index": 27, "context": "The oryx she spotted are certainly too big for a lone cheetah but a coalition of two or three of them could probably take such a big antelope down", "context_len": 29}}}, "acacia": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 16, "context": "Soon after take off , the wind comes up unexpectedly , pushing the balloon towards the acacia forest bordering the plains", "context_len": 21}}}, "thorny": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 4, "context": "A landing in the thorny trees would spell disaster and shred the balloon to pieces", "context_len": 15}}}, "hyenas": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 10, "context": "I have done a lot of work with lions and hyenas , but I never had a chance to observe cheetahs at such close range in the wild before", "context_len": 29}}}, "vantage": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 34, "context": "The next morning , we hooked up with Ishmail , a local guide who took us on game viewing expedition on the river , a great opportunity to observe the wildlife from a unique vantage point", "context_len": 36}}}, "oryx": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 1, "context": "The oryx she spotted are certainly too big for a lone cheetah but a coalition of two or three of them could probably take such a big antelope down", "context_len": 29}}}, "coalition": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 14, "context": "The oryx she spotted are certainly too big for a lone cheetah but a coalition of two or three of them could probably take such a big antelope down", "context_len": 29}}}, "drastically": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 9, "context": "The fences around the parks reduce their hunting range drastically and they often become prey themselves", "context_len": 16}}}, "unquestionably": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 20, "context": "Considering the loss of habitat due to population explosion in Africa and the hunting by local farmers , man is unquestionably the cheetah 's biggest threat", "context_len": 26}}}, "ironically": {"freq": 4, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 4, "word_index": 0, "context": "Ironically , the program has been so successful that the authorities now have to cope with increasing elephant numbers", "context_len": 19}}}, "northern": {"freq": 5, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 5, "word_index": 12, "context": "Leaving Namibia for the Okavango Delta in Botswana , we cross the northern part of the Kalahari desert , the home of some the biggest and most powerful lions in Africa", "context_len": 31}}}, "campsite": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 6, "context": "As we are looking for a campsite along the northern border of the reserve , we come across a coalition of three big male lions", "context_len": 25}}}, "worrisome": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 2, "context": "What is worrisome is that it 's only the beginning stage and he 's already feeling so sick", "context_len": 18}}}, "farmland": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 6, "context": "Lions normally do not hunt on farmland , but the loss of their habitat force them occasionally to raid villages for domestic animals", "context_len": 23}}}, "carcass": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 3, "context": "One on the carcass , and then there is another in the back", "context_len": 13}}}, "marking": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 6, "context": "I mean they should not be marking their territory", "context_len": 9}}}, "lazily": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 1, "context": "Snooze lazily in the shade of a bush", "context_len": 8}}}, "spills": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresT": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 12, "context": "Known as the river that never finds the sea , the Okavango spills billions of liters of water daily in the Kalahari desert , creating one of the most pristine", "context_len": 30}}}, "refuges": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 2, "context": "untouched wildlife refuges in the world", "context_len": 6}}}, "delta": {"freq": 9, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 8, "word_index": 19, "context": "Although the Chobe river is less than 300 km from the Okavango , there are no roads crossing the delta , so we have to drive around the Southern part of the flood plains", "context_len": 34}, "UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 2, "context": "i joined delta gamma", "context_len": 4}}}, "irrigation": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 4, "context": "If some of the irrigation scheme on the drawing board were to materialize , the falls could be totally dry part of the year", "context_len": 24}}}, "dams": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 12, "context": "The pressure to extract water for agriculture irrigation and to build hydro-electrical dams might just prove impossible to withstand in years to come", "context_len": 23}}}, "cycles": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 30, "context": "so we 're back again , and i 'm actually kind of interested to see how these girls are gon na present themselves , 'cause they 've had 13 other cycles to watch this competition unfold", "context_len": 36}}}, "ecosystem": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 17, "context": "Such human interference with the seasonal cycles of the delta would have catastrophic consequences for this unique ecosystem", "context_len": 18}}}, "inland": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 5, "context": "The Okavango is the largest inland delta on earth , but it is very shallow in most parts", "context_len": 18}}}, "flooded": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 6, "context": "15 km wide , it is flooded with one to ten meters of water depending on the time of the year", "context_len": 21}}}, "papyrus": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 10, "context": "The entire valley is covered with a thick layer of papyrus floating on top of the waterbed", "context_len": 17}}}, "meander": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 22, "context": "In the deepest part of the valley where the current is the strongest , the water flow opens up wide channels that meander downstream like giant snakes", "context_len": 27}}}, "downstream": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 23, "context": "In the deepest part of the valley where the current is the strongest , the water flow opens up wide channels that meander downstream like giant snakes", "context_len": 27}, "VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 3, "context": "A few kilometers downstream the Chobe river merges with the mighty Zambezi and lead us to one of the seven wonders of nature ,", "context_len": 24}}}, "islands": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 1, "context": "Small islands pop up everywhere , offering a sanctuary to a great variety of big game animals", "context_len": 17}}}, "herds": {"freq": 10, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 10, "word_index": 27, "context": "But the short-rain season has come early in the East African plains and we are anxious to head to the Serengeti for a chance to see the herds of the great migration", "context_len": 32}}}, "culling": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 5, "context": "The Botswana government is against culling and translocating mass numbers of elephants to other parts of Africa where their numbers are dwindling", "context_len": 22}}}, "dwindling": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 21, "context": "The Botswana government is against culling and translocating mass numbers of elephants to other parts of Africa where their numbers are dwindling", "context_len": 22}}}, "crocodiles": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 11, "context": "Not too close to the water though , there are huge crocodiles in the Chobe", "context_len": 15}}}, "foreground": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 9, "context": "A picture perfect scene , with elephants in the foreground", "context_len": 10}}}, "impalas": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 1, "context": "These impalas are unusually relaxed", "context_len": 5}}}, "unusually": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 3, "context": "These impalas are unusually relaxed", "context_len": 5}}}, "splashing": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 22, "context": "In a few minutes we witness the entire ritual of the elephants ' daily trip to the river , drinking , mud splashing , dusting and socializing !", "context_len": 28}}}, "dusting": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 24, "context": "In a few minutes we witness the entire ritual of the elephants ' daily trip to the river , drinking , mud splashing , dusting and socializing !", "context_len": 28}}}, "privy": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 5, "context": "Minutes later , we become privy to another exciting scene as the herd decided to swim across the river to feed on a patch of tall grass in the middle of the Chobe", "context_len": 33}}}, "merges": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 7, "context": "A few kilometers downstream the Chobe river merges with the mighty Zambezi and lead us to one of the seven wonders of nature ,", "context_len": 24}}}, "embark": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 1, "context": "I embark with Dany on the most daring balloon flight of the journey in the deep canyon over the Zambezi rapids", "context_len": 21}, "NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 1, "context": "Please embark at gate 3", "context_len": 5}}}, "rapids": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 20, "context": "I embark with Dany on the most daring balloon flight of the journey in the deep canyon over the Zambezi rapids", "context_len": 21}}}, "deflate": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 5, "context": "There is no way to deflate the balloon without damaging it", "context_len": 11}}}, "maneuverable": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 7, "context": "If two-seat design makes the balloon more maneuverable and gives it a greater flying range , it also makes the landing much more challenging", "context_len": 24}}}, "unpredictability": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 4, "context": "I actually enjoy the unpredictability of these rough landings", "context_len": 9}}}, "landings": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 8, "context": "We 've scoured the periodicals for other meteorite landings in the last week", "context_len": 13}}}, "lioness": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 5, "context": "I think I saw a lioness down there", "context_len": 8}, "NOUN_P": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 2, "context": "A beautiful lioness and a big male", "context_len": 7}}}, "crater": {"freq": 5, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 5, "word_index": 33, "context": "We are only three hours from the dry Serengeti plains but it feels like we are in the middle of the Amazon and as soon as we get to the edge of the crater it is going to be a totally different landscape", "context_len": 43}}}, "puzzled": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 7, "context": "Perhaps , a surprised look , perhaps puzzled , will appear on your face", "context_len": 14}}}, "mara": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 0, "context": "Mara", "context_len": 1}}}, "rainforest": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 6, "context": "The vegetation below is not a rainforest", "context_len": 7}}}, "rift": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 17, "context": "It seldom rains around here but natural springs that surge up at the foot of the great rift valley escarpment , provide moisture for this lush vegetation to grow", "context_len": 29}}}, "escarpment": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 9, "context": "As soon as we clear the top of the escarpment , we reach the slope of the Ngorongoro crater , the largest volcanic cauldron on earth and one of the most unique African ecosystems", "context_len": 34}}}, "lush": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 25, "context": "It seldom rains around here but natural springs that surge up at the foot of the great rift valley escarpment , provide moisture for this lush vegetation to grow", "context_len": 29}, "NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 1, "context": "A lush", "context_len": 2}}}, "slope": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 14, "context": "As soon as we clear the top of the escarpment , we reach the slope of the Ngorongoro crater , the largest volcanic cauldron on earth and one of the most unique African ecosystems", "context_len": 34}}}, "cauldron": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 23, "context": "As soon as we clear the top of the escarpment , we reach the slope of the Ngorongoro crater , the largest volcanic cauldron on earth and one of the most unique African ecosystems", "context_len": 34}}}, "ecosystems": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 33, "context": "As soon as we clear the top of the escarpment , we reach the slope of the Ngorongoro crater , the largest volcanic cauldron on earth and one of the most unique African ecosystems", "context_len": 34}}}, "teems": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresT": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 8, "context": "Only 20 km in diameter , the crater teems with a great variety of wildlife , making Ngorongoro a miniature version of the Serengeti", "context_len": 24}}}, "wildebeest": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 5, "context": "That 's some herd of wildebeest !", "context_len": 7}, "UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 10, "context": "By the break of dawn the herds of zebras and wildebeest have vanished", "context_len": 13}}}, "zebras": {"freq": 4, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 4, "word_index": 8, "context": "By the break of dawn the herds of zebras and wildebeest have vanished", "context_len": 13}}}, "buffaloes": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 5, "context": "There is a herd of buffaloes , way back there in the sunlight", "context_len": 13}}}, "lionesses": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 5, "context": "Look at that , two lionesses", "context_len": 6}}}, "unsettled": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 11, "context": "The events of last night left everyone on the expedition pretty unsettled", "context_len": 12}}}, "hyena": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 4, "context": "- It 's a hyena !", "context_len": 6}}}, "peaking": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 13, "context": "Mount Kilimanjaro is located in Tanzania right on the border with Kenya , peaking at 5,895 m", "context_len": 17}}}, "shrouded": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 7, "context": "The tallest mountain in Africa is often shrouded with clouds and is not visible for weeks on end", "context_len": 18}}}, "conservation": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 23, "context": "Most of the wildlife at the base of mount Kilimanjaro is found on the Kenyan side of the border , but long term conservation efforts and intense anti-poaching surveillance is paying off", "context_len": 32}}}, "antelopes": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 5, "context": "Large herds of elephants , antelopes and predators have returned to the foothills in Tanzania", "context_len": 15}}}, "foothills": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 12, "context": "Large herds of elephants , antelopes and predators have returned to the foothills in Tanzania", "context_len": 15}}}, "burgeon": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 4, "context": "But as dark clouds burgeon all around the mountain , we know there will be no flying today", "context_len": 18}}}, "glaciers": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 3, "context": "But the melting glaciers at the top of the mountain which will completely disappear before the decade is over are a stark reminder as to how fragile our planet really is", "context_len": 31}}}, "supervises": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresT": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 4, "context": "My friend Damian Bell supervises the anti-poaching efforts around mount Kilimanjaro", "context_len": 11}}}, "stunningly": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 2, "context": "In this stunningly beautiful part of Africa , we can not help but think that despite the great efforts by local governments and NGOs , it is going to be a daunting task to preserve it all", "context_len": 37}}}, "daunting": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, 